  "$comment": "Lot G (answer 144), the website's half (28 Sep 2026): adx.in's features. Every folder under src/app and src/components — and each route file at the root of src/app (the home page, the 404, the sitemap, robots.txt), named as app/<file> — must sit under one of the paths below (scripts/check-features.mjs, run by `npm run lint`); the longest path wins, a bare `app` or `components` is refused because it would cover everything. A key the backend declares in a features.ts, or the apps' manifests already name, only needs its paths — the backend's kind, owner and description carry over and WEBSITE is added to its surfaces; a website-only key (`website.*`) carries all four. `npm run features:sync` in ADX-backendv1 folds this into docs/feature-registry.json beside the console's and the two apps' manifests; the website reads its switches from GET /app/flags (lib/flags.tsx — a website-only key is answered there too), and the kill switches the backend enforces with requireFeature are gated in the pages through `useSwitchedOff` / `FeatureGate` (components/platform/feature-off.tsx) and the API client's 503 FEATURE_OFF mapping. A path may sit under more than one key: the folder belongs to its longest-path feature, and every key that draws a control in it names it. `variants` fold into the registry's list exactly as the apps' do.",
